{ bigdecimals.a68 - the module Bigdecimals of a68j.  Generated by
  tools/gen_bignums.py; do not edit.

  Decimals of any precision, mode Bigdecimal, with the operators of a
  real.  The values are java.math.BigDecimal objects (a68j.jlib.BigDec),
  which never change: an operator yields a new Bigdecimal.  The module
  accesses Bigints publicly, so a program that accesses Bigdecimals can use
  the Bigints as well.

  Every operation rounds its result to the precision, a number of
  significant decimal digits: 70 at the start, as the long long real of
  Algol 68 Genie.  The precision can be changed at any time; the values
  already computed keep their digits.  Rounding is half away from zero.

  A Bigdecimal is a Java object: a name that refers to no Algol 68 value.
  It can be passed around, kept in variables (Bigdecimal x := DEC 1) and
  given to the operators and procedures below, but not dereferenced or
  assigned to.  IS compares the objects, = compares the values (DEC "1.0"
  = DEC "1.00").  For Bigdecimals a and b, a value n of mode int, long int,
  long long int, real, long real, long long real or Bigint, and Bigints i
  and j:

      DEC n, DEC s             the Bigdecimal of n, or of the decimal
                               number in the string s (a sign, digits with
                               or without a point, an exponent with e or E;
                               white space around it), rounded; a real
                               gives its shortest decimal (DEC 0.1 is 0.1)
      TOREAL a, TOLONGREAL a   a as a real or long real; a value beyond the
                               limits is a runtime error
      ROUND a, ENTIER a        the nearest Bigint (half away from zero), the
                               largest Bigint not greater than a
      - a, + a, ABS a          negation, a rounded to the precision, the
                               absolute value
      SIGN a                   -1, 0 or 1
      a + b, a - b, a * b, a / b
                               for a Bigdecimal and a Bigdecimal or n on
                               either side
      i / j                    the quotient as a Bigdecimal, also for i or
                               j an int, long int or long long int
      a = b, a /= b, a < b, a <= b, a > b, a >= b, EQ, NE, LT, LE, GT, GE
                               the same operand modes as a + b
      a ** e, a UP e, a ^ e    the power with an int exponent e, also
                               negative
      x +:= b, x -:= b, x *:= b, x /:= b, PLUSAB, MINUSAB, TIMESAB, DIVAB
                               for a variable x of mode ref Bigdecimal and b
                               a Bigdecimal or n
      bigdec_set_precision (d), bigdec_precision
                               set the precision to d >= 1 digits, and the
                               precision
      bigdec_sqrt (a)          the square root, for a >= 0
      bigdec_whole (a, width), bigdec_fixed (a, width, after),
      bigdec_float (a, width, after, exp)
                               a as a string, with the rules of whole, fixed
                               and float
      bigdec_text (a)          a as a string without exponent and without
                               trailing zeros

  The operators have the priorities of the prelude; the module declares
  none, so a program can access it together with Lists, Hashmaps, Texts
  and Genie_Transput.  A NIL Bigdecimal, a division by zero, a negative
  argument of bigdec_sqrt, a precision below 1 and a text that is not a
  number are runtime errors.

  Example:

      access Bigdecimals (
          bigdec_set_precision (50);
          puts (bigdec_text (bigdec_sqrt (DEC 2)) + "'n")
      )

  Bundled with a68j-backend.jar; a program needs -fnest-java only to
  declare formal holes of its own, not to access this module. }

module Bigdecimals =
access pub Bigints
def
    pub mode Bigdecimal = ref Bigdecimal_object;
    pub mode Bigdecimal_object = struct (int bigdecimal_java_object);

    proc (int) Bigdecimal j_of_int = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.ofLong";
    proc (long int) Bigdecimal j_of_long_int = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.ofLong";
    proc (long long int) Bigdecimal j_of_long_long_int = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.ofLong";
    proc (real) Bigdecimal j_of_real = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.ofFloat";
    proc (long real) Bigdecimal j_of_long_real = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.ofDouble";
    proc (long long real) Bigdecimal j_of_long_long_real = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.ofDouble";
    proc (Bigint) Bigdecimal j_of_bigint = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.ofBigint";
    proc (int) Bigdecimal j_exact_int = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.exactLong";
    proc (long int) Bigdecimal j_exact_long_int = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.exactLong";
    proc (long long int) Bigdecimal j_exact_long_long_int = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.exactLong";
    proc (real) Bigdecimal j_exact_real = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.exactFloat";
    proc (long real) Bigdecimal j_exact_long_real = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.exactDouble";
    proc (long long real) Bigdecimal j_exact_long_long_real = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.exactDouble";
    proc (Bigint) Bigdecimal j_exact_bigint = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.exactBigint";
    proc (string) Bigdecimal j_parse = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.parse";
    proc (Bigdecimal) real j_to_real = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.toFloat";
    proc (Bigdecimal) long real j_to_long_real = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.toDouble";
    proc (Bigdecimal) Bigint j_round = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.round";
    proc (Bigdecimal) Bigint j_entier = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.entier";
    proc (Bigdecimal) Bigdecimal j_plus = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.plus";
    proc (Bigdecimal) Bigdecimal j_negate = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.negate";
    proc (Bigdecimal) Bigdecimal j_abs = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.abs";
    proc (Bigdecimal) int j_sign = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.sign";
    proc (Bigdecimal, Bigdecimal) Bigdecimal j_add = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.add";
    proc (Bigdecimal, Bigdecimal) Bigdecimal j_subtract = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.subtract";
    proc (Bigdecimal, Bigdecimal) Bigdecimal j_multiply = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.multiply";
    proc (Bigdecimal, Bigdecimal) Bigdecimal j_divide = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.divide";
    proc (Bigint, Bigint) Bigdecimal j_divide_bigints = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.divideBigints";
    proc (Bigdecimal, Bigdecimal) int j_compare = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.compare";
    proc (Bigdecimal, int) Bigdecimal j_pow = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.pow";
    proc (int) void j_set_precision = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.setPrecision";
    proc int j_precision = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.precision";
    proc (Bigdecimal) Bigdecimal j_sqrt = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.sqrt";
    proc (Bigdecimal, int) string j_whole = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.whole";
    proc (Bigdecimal, int, int) string j_fixed = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.fixed";
    proc (Bigdecimal, int, int, int) string j_float = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.floating";
    proc (Bigdecimal) string j_text = nest Java "a68j.jlib.BigDec.text";

    { Conversions. }

    pub op DEC = (int n) Bigdecimal: j_of_int (n);
    pub op DEC = (long int n) Bigdecimal: j_of_long_int (n);
    pub op DEC = (long long int n) Bigdecimal: j_of_long_long_int (n);
    pub op DEC = (real n) Bigdecimal: j_of_real (n);
    pub op DEC = (long real n) Bigdecimal: j_of_long_real (n);
    pub op DEC = (long long real n) Bigdecimal: j_of_long_long_real (n);
    pub op DEC = (Bigint n) Bigdecimal: j_of_bigint (n);
    pub op DEC = (string s) Bigdecimal: j_parse (s);
    pub op DEC = (char c) Bigdecimal: j_parse (c);
    pub op TOREAL = (Bigdecimal a) real: j_to_real (a);
    pub op TOLONGREAL = (Bigdecimal a) long real: j_to_long_real (a);
    pub op ROUND = (Bigdecimal a) Bigint: j_round (a);
    pub op ENTIER = (Bigdecimal a) Bigint: j_entier (a);

    { Monadic operators. }

    pub op - = (Bigdecimal a) Bigdecimal: j_negate (a);
    pub op + = (Bigdecimal a) Bigdecimal: j_plus (a);
    pub op ABS = (Bigdecimal a) Bigdecimal: j_abs (a);
    pub op SIGN = (Bigdecimal a) int: j_sign (a);

    { Dyadic operators: two Bigdecimals, or a Bigdecimal and an int, long
      int, long long int, real, long real, long long real or Bigint on
      either side. }

    pub op + = (Bigdecimal a, b) Bigdecimal: j_add (a, b);
    pub op + = (Bigdecimal a, int b) Bigdecimal: j_add (a, j_exact_int (b));
    pub op + = (int a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_add (j_exact_int (a), b);
    pub op + = (Bigdecimal a, long int b) Bigdecimal: j_add (a, j_exact_long_int (b));
    pub op + = (long int a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_add (j_exact_long_int (a), b);
    pub op + = (Bigdecimal a, long long int b) Bigdecimal: j_add (a, j_exact_long_long_int (b));
    pub op + = (long long int a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_add (j_exact_long_long_int (a), b);
    pub op + = (Bigdecimal a, real b) Bigdecimal: j_add (a, j_exact_real (b));
    pub op + = (real a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_add (j_exact_real (a), b);
    pub op + = (Bigdecimal a, long real b) Bigdecimal: j_add (a, j_exact_long_real (b));
    pub op + = (long real a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_add (j_exact_long_real (a), b);
    pub op + = (Bigdecimal a, long long real b) Bigdecimal: j_add (a, j_exact_long_long_real (b));
    pub op + = (long long real a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_add (j_exact_long_long_real (a), b);
    pub op + = (Bigdecimal a, Bigint b) Bigdecimal: j_add (a, j_exact_bigint (b));
    pub op + = (Bigint a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_add (j_exact_bigint (a), b);
    pub op - = (Bigdecimal a, b) Bigdecimal: j_subtract (a, b);
    pub op - = (Bigdecimal a, int b) Bigdecimal: j_subtract (a, j_exact_int (b));
    pub op - = (int a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_subtract (j_exact_int (a), b);
    pub op - = (Bigdecimal a, long int b) Bigdecimal: j_subtract (a, j_exact_long_int (b));
    pub op - = (long int a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_subtract (j_exact_long_int (a), b);
    pub op - = (Bigdecimal a, long long int b) Bigdecimal: j_subtract (a, j_exact_long_long_int (b));
    pub op - = (long long int a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_subtract (j_exact_long_long_int (a), b);
    pub op - = (Bigdecimal a, real b) Bigdecimal: j_subtract (a, j_exact_real (b));
    pub op - = (real a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_subtract (j_exact_real (a), b);
    pub op - = (Bigdecimal a, long real b) Bigdecimal: j_subtract (a, j_exact_long_real (b));
    pub op - = (long real a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_subtract (j_exact_long_real (a), b);
    pub op - = (Bigdecimal a, long long real b) Bigdecimal: j_subtract (a, j_exact_long_long_real (b));
    pub op - = (long long real a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_subtract (j_exact_long_long_real (a), b);
    pub op - = (Bigdecimal a, Bigint b) Bigdecimal: j_subtract (a, j_exact_bigint (b));
    pub op - = (Bigint a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_subtract (j_exact_bigint (a), b);
    pub op * = (Bigdecimal a, b) Bigdecimal: j_multiply (a, b);
    pub op * = (Bigdecimal a, int b) Bigdecimal: j_multiply (a, j_exact_int (b));
    pub op * = (int a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_multiply (j_exact_int (a), b);
    pub op * = (Bigdecimal a, long int b) Bigdecimal: j_multiply (a, j_exact_long_int (b));
    pub op * = (long int a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_multiply (j_exact_long_int (a), b);
    pub op * = (Bigdecimal a, long long int b) Bigdecimal: j_multiply (a, j_exact_long_long_int (b));
    pub op * = (long long int a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_multiply (j_exact_long_long_int (a), b);
    pub op * = (Bigdecimal a, real b) Bigdecimal: j_multiply (a, j_exact_real (b));
    pub op * = (real a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_multiply (j_exact_real (a), b);
    pub op * = (Bigdecimal a, long real b) Bigdecimal: j_multiply (a, j_exact_long_real (b));
    pub op * = (long real a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_multiply (j_exact_long_real (a), b);
    pub op * = (Bigdecimal a, long long real b) Bigdecimal: j_multiply (a, j_exact_long_long_real (b));
    pub op * = (long long real a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_multiply (j_exact_long_long_real (a), b);
    pub op * = (Bigdecimal a, Bigint b) Bigdecimal: j_multiply (a, j_exact_bigint (b));
    pub op * = (Bigint a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_multiply (j_exact_bigint (a), b);
    pub op / = (Bigdecimal a, b) Bigdecimal: j_divide (a, b);
    pub op / = (Bigdecimal a, int b) Bigdecimal: j_divide (a, j_exact_int (b));
    pub op / = (int a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_divide (j_exact_int (a), b);
    pub op / = (Bigdecimal a, long int b) Bigdecimal: j_divide (a, j_exact_long_int (b));
    pub op / = (long int a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_divide (j_exact_long_int (a), b);
    pub op / = (Bigdecimal a, long long int b) Bigdecimal: j_divide (a, j_exact_long_long_int (b));
    pub op / = (long long int a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_divide (j_exact_long_long_int (a), b);
    pub op / = (Bigdecimal a, real b) Bigdecimal: j_divide (a, j_exact_real (b));
    pub op / = (real a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_divide (j_exact_real (a), b);
    pub op / = (Bigdecimal a, long real b) Bigdecimal: j_divide (a, j_exact_long_real (b));
    pub op / = (long real a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_divide (j_exact_long_real (a), b);
    pub op / = (Bigdecimal a, long long real b) Bigdecimal: j_divide (a, j_exact_long_long_real (b));
    pub op / = (long long real a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_divide (j_exact_long_long_real (a), b);
    pub op / = (Bigdecimal a, Bigint b) Bigdecimal: j_divide (a, j_exact_bigint (b));
    pub op / = (Bigint a, Bigdecimal b) Bigdecimal: j_divide (j_exact_bigint (a), b);
    pub op ** = (Bigdecimal a, int e) Bigdecimal: j_pow (a, e);
    pub op UP = (Bigdecimal a, int e) Bigdecimal: j_pow (a, e);
    pub op ^ = (Bigdecimal a, int e) Bigdecimal: j_pow (a, e);

    { The quotient of two Bigints, or of a Bigint and an int, long int or
      long long int on either side. }

    pub op / = (Bigint a, b) Bigdecimal: j_divide_bigints (a, b);
    pub op / = (Bigint a, int b) Bigdecimal: j_divide_bigints (a, BIG b);
    pub op / = (int a, Bigint b) Bigdecimal: j_divide_bigints (BIG a, b);
    pub op / = (Bigint a, long int b) Bigdecimal: j_divide_bigints (a, BIG b);
    pub op / = (long int a, Bigint b) Bigdecimal: j_divide_bigints (BIG a, b);
    pub op / = (Bigint a, long long int b) Bigdecimal: j_divide_bigints (a, BIG b);
    pub op / = (long long int a, Bigint b) Bigdecimal: j_divide_bigints (BIG a, b);

    { Comparisons. }

    pub op = = (Bigdecimal a, b) bool: j_compare (a, b) = 0;
    pub op = = (Bigdecimal a, int b) bool: j_compare (a, j_exact_int (b)) = 0;
    pub op = = (int a, Bigdecimal b) bool: j_compare (j_exact_int (a), b) = 0;
    pub op = = (Bigdecimal a, long int b) bool: j_compare (a, j_exact_long_int (b)) = 0;
    pub op = = (long int a, Bigdecimal b) bool: j_compare (j_exact_long_int (a), b) = 0;
    pub op = = (Bigdecimal a, long long int b) bool: j_compare (a, j_exact_long_long_int (b)) = 0;
    pub op = = (long long int a, Bigdecimal b) bool: j_compare (j_exact_long_long_int (a), b) = 0;
    pub op = = (Bigdecimal a, real b) bool: j_compare (a, j_exact_real (b)) = 0;
    pub op = = (real a, Bigdecimal b) bool: j_compare (j_exact_real (a), b) = 0;
    pub op = = (Bigdecimal a, long real b) bool: j_compare (a, j_exact_long_real (b)) = 0;
    pub op = = (long real a, Bigdecimal b) bool: j_compare (j_exact_long_real (a), b) = 0;
    pub op = = (Bigdecimal a, long long real b) bool: j_compare (a, j_exact_long_long_real (b)) = 0;
    pub op = = (long long real a, Bigdecimal b) bool: j_compare (j_exact_long_long_real (a), b) = 0;
    pub op = = (Bigdecimal a, Bigint b) bool: j_compare (a, j_exact_bigint (b)) = 0;
    pub op = = (Bigint a, Bigdecimal b) bool: j_compare (j_exact_bigint (a), b) = 0;
    pub op /= = (Bigdecimal a, b) bool: j_compare (a, b) /= 0;
    pub op /= = (Bigdecimal a, int b) bool: j_compare (a, j_exact_int (b)) /= 0;
